WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.186
Functions are the heart of R.

2
00:00:03.186 --> 00:00:08.754
In this lesson, you will use five friendly functions to sort and summarize numbers,

3
00:00:08.754 --> 00:00:12.731
and you will see one function that does something surprising.

4
00:00:12.731 --> 00:00:14.720
Let's explore them together, slowly.

5
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.768
Here are the functions from our list. First, sort.

6
00:00:19.768 --> 00:00:23.992
It puts our numbers in order, from the smallest to the largest.

7
00:00:23.992 --> 00:00:28.920
In the console, we see one, three, three, all the way up to five

8
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.680
thousand four hundred thirty three.

9
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:31.852
Next, sum.

10
00:00:31.852 --> 00:00:34.484
Notice, sum does not even need c.

11
00:00:34.484 --> 00:00:37.116
You can give it the numbers directly.

12
00:00:37.116 --> 00:00:40.500
The total is five thousand five hundred ninety four.

13
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:46.851
Now length.

14
00:00:46.851 --> 00:00:49.479
Length counts how many values we have.

15
00:00:49.479 --> 00:00:54.360
I type length, open the brackets, and inside, c with the same numbers.

16
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:16.788
Run it.

17
00:01:16.788 --> 00:01:18.164
The answer is fifteen.

18
00:01:18.164 --> 00:01:19.540
We have fifteen numbers.

19
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.200
Next, mean, which is the average.

20
00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.700
And median, the middle value when the numbers are sorted.

21
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:55.091
When I first ran mode, I got an error: unused arguments.

22
00:01:55.091 --> 00:01:58.357
That is because I forgot c around the numbers.

23
00:01:58.357 --> 00:02:01.260
So I add c, and run it again.

24
00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.946
The mean is three hundred seventy two point nine three.

25
00:02:24.946 --> 00:02:31.100
That is high, because one number, five thousand four hundred thirty three, pulls the average up.

26
00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.826
The median is only five.

27
00:02:37.826 --> 00:02:43.694
When a few values are very big, the median gives a better picture of the typical value.

28
00:02:43.694 --> 00:02:46.800
That is a useful lesson for any data work.

29
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.962
And mode? It says numeric.

30
00:02:48.962 --> 00:02:54.248
In R, mode tells you the type of the data, not the most common value.

31
00:02:54.248 --> 00:02:57.420
A small surprise, and a good one to remember.

32
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:08.569
Finally, I scroll back to the top of our script.

33
00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:11.251
Look how much we wrote today.

34
00:03:11.251 --> 00:03:15.720
Calculations, data types, variables, vectors, comparisons, and functions. Excellent work!

